# daemon on -- same contract as lifecycle-journal's own env: this driver
# reboots a fresh master/worker generation between its QUIT and TERM phases
# (start_phase REBOOT=1), and the daemon-off alternative tracks the master by
# $! -- reaped the instant the master forks away, useless for retargeting
# THIS generation's own master a moment later. PROBER_DAEMON_MODE=on's
# pidfile-based tracking, re-exported by driver.sh before it calls
# prober_boot a second time, is what makes that second boot reliable.
PROBER_DAEMON_MODE=on
